#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:5
#: 83d5cc92ffbe47d6a3aa505a08b4f556
msgid "DroneCAN GUI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:7
#: 30b281f108ca4185bd3a12f63d3db5b5
msgid "DroneCAN_GUI is a tool that allows viewing, configuration and software updates of nodes connected to the BUS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:10
#: 04f085e126064238bcb82f6f8eadf4c7
msgid "Windows: Download `DroneCAN_GUI <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/CAN_GUI/>`_ and install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:11
#: c24b2a891a7848919371369278ba8e2c
msgid "Linux: python3 -m pip install dronecan_gui_tool dronecan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:13
#: c53c3b16fea04d33bac397e48fa7f239
msgid "Before the autopilot can be connected, SLCAN mode must be operational. See :ref:`common-slcan-f4` or :ref:`common-slcan-f7h7` for setup information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:15
#: 02a1db9a5a0a442ea4e58e8ace536944
msgid "Start DroneCAN GUI and select the correct USB port for the SLCAN interface. The default CAN bus bit rate of 1,000,000 won't  need to be changed unless the :ref:`CAN_P1_BITRATE<CAN_P1_BITRATE>` or :ref:`CAN_P2_BITRATE<CAN_P2_BITRATE>` (if using the second autopilot CAN port) has been changed. The Adapter baud rate should match the autopilot's SERIALx port baud rate. The default value of 115.2KBaud should be correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:17
#: 70981e12b27e41f1afd55effbd51099c
msgid "Almost all ArduPilot autopilots use VCP USB connections and Adapter port baud rate value is irrelevant and can be any value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:21
#: c36698eec65b44ccb9ea1db082d100f2
msgid "DroneCAN_GUI tool will start with an interface as the image below. Click on tick box next to Local node ID. Leave it unchanged, unless you have another node on the CANBUS with the same address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:26
#: 32a55ecfea3d49648b66f7211d9abc09
msgid "If the node has a bootloader only installed, then firmware will need to be uploaded. ``MAINTENANCE`` will be displayed. Firmware can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/AP_Periph/>`__ and downloaded for the node.  Click on the button lower right and then double click on ``org.ardupilot.ap_periph`` as highlighted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:31
#: 548d02d728a94fdb9637a82b0af4d5b8
msgid "The following pop up window will appear. Click on update firmware and select the correct file for the node connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:33
#: 9453a8c61e634ac5bd2dd84f49c6594d
msgid "If you have trouble updating firmware, trying renaming the firmware filename to something very short, such as \"a.bin\". Longer filenames sometimes have difficulty loading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:38
#: ce33fa34e4ff4a67956a8b54e63f9d3d
msgid "Once the firmware has finished uploading to node the main window will change to ``OPERATIONAL`` as per image below. Press the ``Fetch All`` button, and double click on the FLASH_BOOTLOADER parameter and enter 1 in the highlighted box. Press ``Send`` and close the dialog. The address of the node can be changed in this window to avoid conflict with another node on the CANBUS, as well as any DroneCAN device specific parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:42
#: 09ae5c612098444cbe09bc5fed06c505
msgid "A debug message will show complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:46
#: d09926bbf350484fada0dfd87b8ebc73
msgid "Messages coming through the CANBUS can be viewed using the bus monitor tool in \"Tools\" menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-gui.rst:50
#: 96f7e3f4f4a14e61b45884d3fc9fdb3b
msgid "To return to normal operation, close the DroneCAN_GUI tool."
msgstr ""
